---
layout: layouts/base.njk
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
pagination:
  data: composedPages
  size: 1
  alias: pageComposition
permalink: "{{ pageComposition.target.route }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ pageComposition.target.title }}"
---
{# Production rendering of published standalone pages (Phase 6.5, #32-T7).
   One page per composedPages entry, paginated size:1, generated at the entry's
   single-segment root route (e.g. /my-page/) — same root-generation shape as
   categories.njk. An empty composedPages array (no published pages / ENOENT)
   yields ZERO pages, which is correct: nothing is emitted and the build does
   not crash. The build-time slug-guard (composedPages.mjs) has already filtered
   out any route colliding with an authored content/pages/<slug>.md page.

   Pages are FULL-PAGE compositions (the tree carries its own hero/main/sidebar/
   footer structure), so this mirrors preview-pages.njk: a direct shortcode call,
   NEVER via {% include %} (Eleventy 3.1.2 silently drops async shortcode output
   inside {% include %}). The shortcode owns the schemaVersion 4 + tree gates and
   degrades to an HTML comment on invalid artifacts.

   target.title is operator input: it reaches <title>/OG via the autoescaped
   `title` front-matter binding above — NEVER rendered with `| safe` (stored-XSS
   defense).

   The `data-indiekit-composed-page` marker below identifies this output as a
   composed page so the orphan prune (lib/prune-composed-pages.mjs) can safely
   remove a deleted/renamed page's stale /<slug>/ output WITHOUT risking authored
   pages or collection listings in the shared root namespace. It is an attribute
   (not an HTML comment) so it survives the production htmlmin removeComments
   pass. #}
<div data-indiekit-composed-page hidden></div>
{% renderCompositionTree pageComposition %}
